====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
   best p by (budget, M):

      budget      M=16    M=32    M=64
   ----------------------------------------------------
        16384    0.25    0.25    0.50
       262144    0.50    0.50    0.50

  If the best p FALLS as M grows, the shipped constant is a schedule in
  disguise and v110's growing gap is partly self-inflicted - the rescale
  keeps buying down a bias that stopped being the binding constraint.

  If p=0.50 wins everywhere, the rescale is right and V6's large-M deficit
  is structural: reading M components from G circuits costs a linearisation
  whose price grows with M, and no choice of radius escapes it.

  NOT MEASURED HERE: converged energy. A larger radius can improve gradient
  DIRECTION while degrading the optimisation, because grad_step takes its
  step size from the same schedule. Any p adopted on this evidence must be
  re-checked on the benchmark before it becomes a default.
